God Himself; Christ; the assembly of the first-born, such as the Apostles; Angels; and the spirits of the just. This being the case, no wonder the text actually speaks of the Church as heaven upon earth, saying that God " hath quickened us together with Christ, .... and hath raised us up together, and made us sit together in heavenly places in Christ Jesus." Wiiat, then, the visible Temple was to the Jews, such

